{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Pan bread: water, mixing and proof time",
  "notes": "Development of a white pan bread (straight dough, 450 g dough pieces, baked 25 min at 220 °C). Water addition, spiral-mixer time and final proof time were varied in a central composite design run on two baking days (factorial points on day 1, axial points on day 2, centre points on both). The bakery switched to a new flour delivery partway through the trial; the lot used for each dough is recorded. Loaf volume was measured by rapeseed displacement 2 h after baking, crumb firmness by texture analyser (25 % compression of a 25 mm slice, day 1) and overall liking by a panel of 10 trained assessors on a 9-point hedonic scale (mean score).",
